"text": "A small, forked tree, its two prongs like a stag's antlers, that roots on bare rocky crowns where little else grows. Its use is a matter of custom rather than craft: climb up, cut a branch, burn it, and rub the cool ashes on the skin. Marked so, a person is held to be safe from any spirit that would ride them, and those who must go into haunted places or deal with the spirit-touched do not go without it.",
