"text": "A lily found only singly, in the quiet backwaters of rivers and streams where the current does not reach, never in a bed and never two together. Country folk hold that breathing the smoke of its burnt petals clears the head and shows the truth of whatever trouble is at hand; those with a hard choice before them sometimes go looking for one. A tincture of the flower makes a lovely perfume that finds ready buyers, which is another reason the lotus is rarely found where people walk often.",
